{
  "_readme": [
    "Traits: desc (shown in tooltips), fx (merged into the effect engine, js/logic/fx.js), plus flags.",
    "fx vocabulary (only these keys): maxEnergy(add) energyRec(mul) actEnergy(mul) actEnergyBy{service:mul} actQuality{service:mul} actBan[service ids] lustBuild(mul) svcLustBuild(flag: giving services to clients build her lust) lustDrop(mul) lustMax(add) lustFloor(add) recklessAt(add) noReckless(flag) moodDrift(mul) moodDelta(mul) moodLoss(mul, only on negative mood changes) moodRest(add) trustGain(mul) skillGain(mul) statGain(mul) lewdGain(mul) jobBonus{job:mul} clientFee(mul) classBonus{class:mul} appeal(add) propRate(mul) security(add) energyBank(add) wardrobe(add) willing(add) rep(mul) promote(mul) tidy(mul) encore(add) stats{stat:add, 0-100 scale; a bonus on top of her trained stats that can exceed the cap} teach(mul: how much she passes on when teaching a class or coaching as madame) learn(mul: how much she picks up from a teacher or the madame).",
    "gen: can be rolled for generic ladies. hidden: not shown until Appraisal Lv 3. story / personal: set by the game, not rolled. excl: traits she can't have together.",
    "earn: lets a lady DEVELOP the trait. {count:'massage', at:40} (w.counts.<key>, e.g. svc, massage, dance, bar, promo, rowdy, rescued, encore, weeksWorked, privateSam, gifts, or svcByAct.<service id>, jobWeeks.<job id>, warm = warm-ups given as a host, hosted = waiting clients entertained as a host, taught = ladies she taught or coached, +1 per lady per week as teacher or madame), {stat:'popularity', at:70} (stats and skills are compared on the 0-100 scale), {trust:90}, {lewd:80}, {weeks:30} (total weeks worked), {job:'dancer', weeks:12}. Checked weekly; once eligible she has earnChance per week to develop it.",
    "ngOnly: generic trait only rolled from cycle 2 (New Game+). ngPerk: offered to carried-over ladies in New Game+. Other agents will expand this catalogue: keep the schema.",
    "Named ladies (characters.json / guests.json) may carry a personal 'unique': {name, desc, fx} (fx merged like a trait; shown on her sheet) and a 'body': {bust, height, figure} (ids from data/body.json; default medium / average / slim)."
  ],
